      },
      "lineNbr": 2335,
      "author": {
        "id": 1606087
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-11T23:20:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are there battery, performance implications to using a PendingIntent here as opposed to sendMessageDelayed?  I ask because of the case where we have rapid delays during reconnect and worried that it could drain the device.  If that\u0027s the case, then you could check the delay and see if you should just directly call sendMessageDelayedwith EVENT_DATA_RECONNECT.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2335,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 2335,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "f8a85c9e4c532c787ae7f6e48acf831cb70b7b3b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d12649d_b70c1761",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/dataconnection/DcTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2335,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T01:03:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are you saying if it\u0027s a short retry we use sendMessageDelayed and if it\u0027s long we use AlarmManager? But what is short what is long?\n\nBattery impact is something we have to be aware of. I remember there were bugs that device keeps waking up during the night. Need to find out the original bug.",
      "parentUuid": "45f7966d_8c475756",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2335,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 2335,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "f8a85c9e4c532c787ae7f6e48acf831cb70b7b3b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb997863_4a57daf6",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/dataconnection/DcTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2335,
      "author": {
        "id": 1606087
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-12T01:19:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I am saying that.  It\u0027s arbitrary but it\u0027s something.  30 seconds?\n\nI bet you it\u0027s the networkUnwanted bug.  The delay was very small and so it drained the battery.  (I\u0027m assuming that sendMessageDelayed keeps the phone on.)\n\nI now see that alarm manager was originally there which makes the change less scary to me.  It still might not be a bad idea to consider.",
      "parentUuid": "4d12649d_b70c1761",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2335,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 2335,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "f8a85c9e4c532c787ae7f6e48acf831cb70b7b3b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "126e5d64_8ffa7d4e",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/dataconnection/DcTracker.java",
